    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `membershipTier`: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\n`membershipTier` is a derived response field (like the existing `membershipNumber`, `displayName`, `initials`), so I added it where those live rather than on the entity:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing the tier:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n   The null/blank guards keep it safe for owners without an email or namesake count.\n\nResults: both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
